    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "I see math as a creative tool rather than a rigid set of rules. As a photography enthusiast, I appreciate how patterns and proportions in math mirror the visual arts. While I enjoy applying it to real-world problems, I don’t consider it my strongest subject—more of a side interest that sparks curiosity.",
    "Do you ever get anxious when thinking about mathematics?": "I rarely feel anxious about math because I approach it with curiosity, not pressure. My background in art and philosophy helps me think abstractly, which makes complex concepts feel approachable. I’d rather tackle problems with patience than rush through them.",
