    "According to you, how can LLMs be used to innovate math learning in schools and universities?": "LLMs can personalize learning by adapting to each student’s pace and style. For example, they could generate interactive problems tailored to a student’s weaknesses, or explain concepts through relatable analogies from art or philosophy. This makes math less intimidating and more engaging for diverse learners."
